<section class="sound-section section-wrap" aria-labelledby="sound-title">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow">About the project</p>
    <h2 id="sound-title">A side project<br><em>by Ben Farrell.</em></h2>
  </div>
  <div>
    <p>I'm a keyboard player trying my best but my favorite music has some sort of strumming guitar. So, also being also a UX nerd, I set out to see if I could recreate without actually having to learn to play a guitar. Maybe this wasn't the most efficient way to tackle this problem, but I certainly had fun.</p>
    <p>Start with a supported drawing tablet, a computer, and a MIDI synth or DAW to send to. Thanks to the <a href="https://opentabletdriver.net">OpenTabletDriver</a> project, most drawing tablets are supported (but be skeptical, I don't have hard facts to back up that claim)</p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/about/">More about the project &amp; some demos <span aria-hidden="true">&nearr;</span></a>
  </div>
</section>

